## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: gameState object; mulberry32() used for all randomness (no Math.random() found); endTurn() calls updateResources→updateColonists→checkAshstorm→fireEvent→trade in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map**: 8x8 map[] from rng() in generateMap(); buildBuilding() checks building.terrain.includes(tile.terrain); adjacencyMult in resolveProduction() alters output via getTileAdjacencies(). Score 2.

**F3 — Economy**: chains power→water(condenser)→food(greenhouse), ruins→parts/metal(scavenger)→scrip(lab); caps enforced and overflow logged in updateResources(). Score 2.

**F4 — Population**: colonist records w/ skill,fatigue,morale,job; skill read via skillBonus in resolveProduction(), but fatigue never read by production code. Score 1.

**F5 — Needs**: food/water consumed in updateColonists(); shortage cuts morale -15; recovery exists (fatigue/morale drift); but morale never multiplies production output anywhere. Score 1.

**F6 — Research**: 8 nodes in RESEARCH_TREE; prereq/cost enforced in researchAvailable()/doResearch(); but 'mining'(unlocks nonexistent 'ore-mine'), 'morale-boost', 'trade-hub' have no effect anywhere in code. Score 1.

**F7 — Events**: 10 EVENTS entries; selection is uniform `EVENTS[floor(rng()*len)]`, not weighted; ≥4 events have differing choice effects; recentEvents Set caps at 4 (cooldown). Score 1.

**F8 — Trade**: updateTradeprices() reads gameState.globalSupply (drifts via tradeResource); tradeInventory limited per session; buy/sell both mutate resources/scrip/supply. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard**: checkAshstorm/triggerAshstorm scale severity with turn, reduced by ashfilter research & watchtowers, repairBuilding spends parts; but resolveProduction() never reads b.health/b.damaged, so damage never reduces output. Score 1.

**F10 — Save/load**: serializeGame()→JSON text in textarea; deserializeGame() JSON.parse in try/catch, alert() on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions**: checkEndConditions() returns win/lose, both reachable; calculateScore() uses turn/population/research/scrip; renderEndScreen() shows summary. Score 2.

**F12 — UI**: switchTab()/state.currentTab wired to buttons; event-turn shows entry.turn; keydown listener for Space/1-5; @media(max-width:600px) present; but .tooltip CSS/tooltipBonus field never rendered anywhere. Score 1.

**F13 — Dev panel**: runTests() has 15 real invariant checks (caps, jobs, terrain, prereqs, PRNG determinism, save/load roundtrip); runBenchmark() runs 200 headless endTurn() calls, returns gameStateHash(). Score 2.

**G1**: researchDone.has('hydroponics'/'smelting-adv'/'industry') read directly in resolveProduction()'s researchBonus multiplier, applied every turn. Score 4.

**G2**: shortage sets morale-=15 in updateColonists(), but resolveProduction() has no morale term; only extreme case (morale≤0 → colonist splice) reduces workers/output. Score 2.

**G3**: triggerAshstorm() sets b.health/b.damaged; resolveProduction() never checks health/damaged so output loss link is absent; repairBuilding() restores health but nothing was actually being lost in production. Score 1.

**G4**: updateTradeprices() formula reads gameState.globalSupply; tradeResource() mutates globalSupply on buy/sell each caravan visit; prices shown in trade UI. Score 4.

**G5**: refugee choice mutates gs.population/colonists.push; colonist-sick choices durably alter morale vs fatigue differently — real state writes, not just log. Score 4.

